//media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--qPvKM23u--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2009","num_upvotes":117,"num_comments":19,"created_at":"2026-04-13T19:03:20.339Z"},{"id":"mx7yroARg","title":"If your validation already controls what data comes in, what is `$fillable` actually protecting you from?\n\nI stopped using it. Here's why.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/if-your-validation-already-controls-what-data-comes-in-what-is-fillable-actually-protecting-you--mx7yroarg","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":48,"num_comments":12,"created_at":"2026-04-09T05:36:37.458Z"},{"id":"NuhGxUVQ6","title":"Laravel Wow","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/laravel-wow-nuhgxuvq6","summary":"Two new features in the Laravel Wow VSCode extension: a PHP Class Organizer that automatically groups methods by visibility and sorts class members, and a Laravel File Generator that lets you run artisan make commands directly from VSCode without switching to the terminal. Covers keyboard shortcuts, configuration options, and a fix for a missing php-parser dependency.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--YtyJycWo--/f_auto/v1774154900/posts/VYgnwwftd?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":13,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-29T05:52:56.251Z"},{"id":"0HO0u0zaW","title":"What questions do you ask when being interviewed?","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-questions-do-you-ask-when-being-interviewed--0ho0u0zaw","summary":"A developer seeks advice on strategic questions to ask during job interviews to evaluate potential employers. The post includes sample questions about deployment processes, database management, and team pain points, aiming to help candidates identify red flags and assess company technical practices before accepting offers.","image":null,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-09-13T07:11:26.069Z"},{"id":"BIiRNYl7J","title":"JSX Edition of Laravel React Starter Kit, Auto-Generated & Ready","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/jsx-edition-of-laravel-react-starter-kit-auto-generated-ready-biirnyl7j","summary":"A JavaScript/JSX version of Laravel's official React starter kit is now available as an automatically generated template. While the official Laravel React starter kit uses TypeScript by default, this alternative provides the same functionality using JavaScript/JSX for developers who prefer not to use TypeScript. The template is kept up to date through automated conversion from the original TypeScript version.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--zPZWRLHv--/f_auto/v1756146921/posts/jDFJ44h2J?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":24,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-08-26T06:34:29.833Z"},{"id":"0wZGpD9nY","title":"Nginx vs Caddy Performance \ud83d\ude2e","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/nginx-vs-caddy-performance--0wzgpd9ny","summary":"A performance comparison between Nginx and Caddy web servers reveals surprising results that could impact server architecture decisions for PHP and Laravel applications. The benchmark results were unexpected and may influence how developers choose between these web servers for their projects.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--8_mUv9QV--/f_auto/v1751654238/posts/KXivNfPrl?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":110,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2025-07-05T12:17:28.428Z"},{"id":"afZ0L6FDb","title":"Laravel 10 JWT Authentication: Secure Login & API Tokens","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/laravel-10-jwt-authentication-secure-login-api-tokens-afz0l6fdb","summary":"A tutorial covering JWT (JSON Web Token) authentication implementation in Laravel 10, focusing on secure user login and API token management. The content demonstrates how to set up JWT-based authentication for API endpoints, handle token generation and validation, and implement secure login mechanisms in Laravel applications.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--EbKILPDP--/f_auto/v1751272233/posts/WRuTH2Pw0?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":17,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2025-06-30T10:39:44.380Z"},{"id":"9IMC4m5Fb","title":"Nuno Interviews Jeffrey Way","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/nuno-interviews-jeffrey-way-9imc4m5fb","summary":"An interview featuring Jeffrey Way, founder of Laracasts and renowned programming educator known for his engaging teaching style. The discussion likely covers his approach to creating educational content and building effective learning experiences for developers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--_B2vz1yq--/f_auto/v1750331891/posts/VXDWK47au?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2025-06-20T06:27:31.345Z"},{"id":"OAlndtdZa","title":"Precise Number Formatting with Laravel's Enhanced Number::spell Method","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/precise-number-formatting-with-laravel-s-enhanced-number-spell-method-oalndtdza","summary":"Laravel has enhanced its Number::spell method by introducing 'until' and 'after' parameters that give developers the flexibility to decide when numbers should appear as words or digits in their applications. This feature supports typographic best practices, making it easier to follow conventions such as spelling out smaller numbers while keeping larger values as digits, thus improving content readability in various applications.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--SLlTfqwr--/f_auto/v1747029196/posts/mxUdbHoiM?_a=BAMClqUq0","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-05-12T09:05:20.277Z"},{"id":"KxwgNjJOG","title":"You are significantly better off as a software engineer if other people know about you.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/you-are-significantly-better-off-as-a-software-engineer-if-other-people-know-about-you--kxwgnjjog","summary":"Visibility in the tech industry is crucial for attracting opportunities, collaborations, and partnerships. By sharing your work and journey, you become known to the right people, reducing the need to pursue every opportunity. Building leverage involves being good at your craft while ensuring you're recognized by those who matter.","image":null,"num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2025-04-29T14:07:36.071Z"}],"similar_handles":["everythingastro","sknexus","thedevcraft","devtools","dailyopensourcetools"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hwchase17","hamelhusain","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"ee903b3d-a9e4-47e2-9631-525a9022cb7f","handle":"everythingastro","name":"Everything Astro","is_squad":true,"x":-8.4151,"y":10.326,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":15,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--PUG86LZ0--/f_auto/v1747800948/squads/ee903b3d-a9e4-47e2-9631-525a9022cb7f?_a=BAMClqUq0","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.543702,"median_upvotes":9.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":1.533333,"tag_diversity":1.333333},"top_tags_preview":[["astro",13],["webdev",12],["tailwind-css",5]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[7.5441,8.2206],"cadence_depth":[-8.9559,-8.3529],"hype_variety":[-8.1471,-6.3382],"title_style":[9.2647,-7.0147]}},{"id":"9a9c19fc-3507-4006-9c8c-41dcd65df3a1","handle":"sknexus","name":"SK NEXUS","is_squad":true,"x":-8.3608,"y":10.2031,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":56,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--osSikTRJ--/f_auto/v1746235502/squads/9a9c19fc-3507-4006-9c8c-41dcd65df3a1","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.834947,"median_upvotes":2.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.026786,"avg_read_time":1.678571,"tag_diversity":1.375},"top_tags_preview":[["hardware",16],["iot",7],["arm",6]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.7059,9.0441],"cadence_depth":[-3.6912,-8.1471],"hype_variety":[6.2353,7.5882],"title_style":[9.7206,4.8824]}},{"id":"db9d9c61-7296-4ef0-9d4d-62dc93b197fa","handle":"t